{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":4378433,"ns":0,"title":"Argument from incredulity","extract":"Argument from incredulity, also known as argument from personal incredulity, appeal to common sense, or the divine fallacy, is a fallacy in informal logic.  It asserts that a proposition must be false because it contradicts one's personal expectations or beliefs, or is difficult to imagine.","description":"Informal logical fallacy","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}